== Secret Quests ==

* The windmill near the middle of the island has 5 ropes attached to the blades. Cut the 5 ropes with any sword M1 to free the windmill.
* After waiting an unspecified amount of time at Pirate Village, a message will appear in chat saying: '''[[System Messages|''"Trouble has broken out at the tavern!"'']]'''  Breach the tavern door, there will be 3 [[Tavern Pirate|Tavern Pirates]] causing trouble in the bottom floor of the tavern where [[Chef]] spawns. Defeating them will have the Tavern Owner thank and give the player a weird brew.  After completing the quest, a message will appear in chat saying:  '''[[System Messages|''"(Roblox username) threw the punks out of the tavern!"'']]'''
* When [[Chef]] awakens, a message will appear in chat saying:  '''[[System Messages|''"A curious smell is brewing from the Chef's kitchen at Pirate Village."'']]'''  Go to the second floor of the tavern and find the cauldron. Place the materials into the cauldron and the boss sequence will start.  After they are defeated, a message will appear in chat saying:  '''[[System Messages|''"(Roblox username) served the awakened Chef his last meal!"'']]'''

== Chest Locations ==
There are three [[Chests|Gold Chests]] and one [[Chests|Diamond Chest]]. The [[Chests|Gold Chest]] is near the [[Rich Man]], the other [[Chests|Gold Chest]] is in [[Chef]]'s house, the last [[Chests|Gold Chest]] is above the [[Set Home Point]] NPC which is the bridge, and the [[Chests|Diamond Chest]] is on the arch at the entrance to the island, being obstructed by boxes.

==Port==
The port of the Pirate Village is a medium-sized port with two docks meant to accommodate players of level 30-60. The port is able to handle two ships at a time. The port is located on the southern end of the island.

==Trivia==
* Most players in [[First Sea]] often go chest hunting on Pirate Village due to the amount of [[chests]] that can be found there.
* All of the enemies use [[swords]], so it is recommended to use [[Blade]] because of its sword immunity.
** A great alternative is any [[elemental]] fruit, like [[Smoke]], [[Ice]], [[Flame]], [[Dark]], [[Light]], or [[Magma]] due to their simple obtainability and AoE skills.

